\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Constants of the final method not stated in the text. Some were revised after development runs (mainly seed 11, \Cref {sec:fix}); all were fixed before the final runs and none was tuned systematically.\relax }}{21}{table.caption.9}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Main results on all 101 tasks in the manifest order (single run per arm). Yes, Partial, No and Start failed are percentages of the 647 test cases; Accuracy $=$ Yes $+\,0.5\times $ Partial. Appearance is the mean grade over all 101 tasks (1--5; tasks without a working site count as 0). Paired $\Delta $ is the mean per-task difference to No Memory with a 95\% bootstrap \gls {ci}; it can differ from the difference of pooled accuracies because tasks have different numbers of test cases. Zero: tasks where every test case fails.\relax }}{23}{table.caption.10}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Prompt content by segment (tasks 1--30 / 31--60 / 61--101).\relax }}{24}{table.caption.12}%
